<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Big Three (World War II)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Big Three were the principal Allied powers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, the United Kingdom, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, and their leaders <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill">Winston Churchill</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franklin-d-roosevelt">Franklin D. Roosevelt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-stalin">Joseph Stalin</a>. At the conferences of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a> in 1943 and Yalta and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potsdam">Potsdam</a> in 1945 they coordinated strategy and shaped the post-war settlement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/big-three-world-war-ii.jpg" alt="Big Three (World War II)" width="320" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franklin D. Roosevelt Library Public Domain Photographs · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tehran_Conference_1943.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
